---
import { url } from '../lib/nav';
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Section from '../components/docs/Section.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro';
---
<Doc
  title="Getting started"
  eyebrow="Start"
  lead="Aurora ships as tokens, React components, and a Figma library, all generated from one source. Pick the entry point that matches how you work."
>
  <Section id="designers" n="01" title="For designers">
    <p>Open the <a href={url('/resources/figma')}>Figma library</a> and enable it for your team. Variables and text styles match the code names exactly, so a colour called <code>text/secondary</code> in Figma is <code>--au-text-secondary</code> in CSS.</p>
    <p>Start from the <a href={url('/principles')}>principles</a>. Every component page then follows the same order, so once you have read one you know where everything is on the rest.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="tokens" n="02" title="Tokens only">
    <p>If you only want the look, use the generated stylesheet. It defines every token as a CSS custom property on <code>:root</code>, plus a class for each type style.</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="html" label="HTML" code={`<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://izaias.xyz/aurora/design/tokens/aurora.css" />

<p class="au-type-title">You landed at six.</p>
<p style="color: var(--au-text-secondary)">There are three hours at eleven.</p>`} />
    <p>The same values are available as <a href={url('/tokens/aurora.tokens.json')}>W3C design tokens JSON</a> for your own pipeline, and as <a href={url('/tokens/figma-variables.json')}>Figma variables JSON</a>.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="react" n="03" title="React components">
    <p>Components are plain React with one CSS file each, in <code>src/components/aurora</code>. They read only semantic tokens, so they follow any change to the source. They are not published to npm yet: copy the folder into your project with the generated <code>tokens.css</code>, or import it directly in a monorepo.</p>
    <CodeBlock tabs={[
      { label: 'Usage', lang: 'tsx', code: `import { SuggestionCard, Gap, Timeline } from './aurora';
import './styles/tokens.css';

export function Afternoon() {
  return (
    <Timeline>
      <Gap time="11.00" span="Three hours">
        <SuggestionCard
          because="Nothing needs you until two."
          what="Contrast and lymphatic recovery, 75 minutes."
          signals={[{ key: 'Calendar', value: 'Clear 11.00 to 14.00' }]}
          onConfirm={book}
        />
      </Gap>
    </Timeline>
  );
}` },
      { label: 'Copy', lang: 'bash', code: `git clone https://github.com/iziuqo/aurora-inspiration
cp -r aurora-inspiration/design-system/src/components/aurora ./src/aurora
cp aurora-inspiration/design-system/src/styles/tokens.css ./src/styles/` },
    ]} />
    <p>Fonts are Newsreader and Nunito Sans, both open licence. Install them from <a href="https://fontsource.org">Fontsource</a> or Google Fonts; the token stacks fall back to system serifs and sans-serifs until they load.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="repo" n="04" title="How the repository is laid out">
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" label="Tree" code={`design-system/
├─ tokens/                 # the source of truth (DTCG JSON)
│  ├─ primitives.json      # raw values: night, stone, aurora, space, easing
│  └─ semantic.json        # named jobs that point at primitives
├─ scripts/
│  ├─ build-tokens.mjs     # writes CSS, TypeScript and Figma variables
│  └─ check-tokens.mjs     # fails the build on contrast or raw colours
├─ src/components/aurora/  # the components, one TSX and one CSS each
└─ src/pages/              # this documentation site`} />
  </Section>
</Doc>
